", "rxn_008", "rxn_009"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_002", "mol_008", "mol_011", "mol_012", "mol_013"]}, {"pathway_id": "P7", "name": "Concentrated glyoxylate aza-Cannizzaro pathway", "description": "Supplied glyoxylate and buffered ammonium undergo internally balanced hydride transfer, producing glycine together with oxamate. The pathway requires neither cyanide nor an external reductant but begins at a concentrated glyoxylate boundary whose origin is not closed by this network.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_013"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_015"]}, {"pathway_id": "P8", "name": "Hydrogen-nickel reductive-amination pathway", "description": "Supplied glyoxylate and ammonia form a transient imine in situ. Nickel-bearing metal catalyzes its reduction by molecular hydrogen in a cool, pressurized, cyanide-free interface. H2 and reactive Ni are boundary resources; glyoxylate synthesis is not assumed.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_010", "rxn_011"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_015", "mol_016"]}, {"pathway_id": "P9", "name": "Reduced FeS-Fe0 reductive-amination pathway", "description": "Supplied glyoxylate and ammonia form the imine, which is reduced by a finite inventory of low-valence iron in an active FeS-Fe0 assemblage. The pathway adopts the demonstrated near-room-temperature organic chemistry without assuming that natural vents automatically generate the laboratory-pretreated material.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_010", "rxn_012"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_015", "mol_016"]}, {"pathway_id": "P10", "name": "Nitrate-fed ferroan-brucite pathway", "description": "Ferroan brucite reduces supplied nitrate to ammonia, enabling in situ condensation with supplied glyoxylate; further mineral reducing equivalents yield glycine. The sequence expresses chemical dependencies within a coupled suspension rather than separate completed batch operations. Dissolved glycine and mineral-associated glycine must be accounted for separately, and no unmodeled acid digestion is credited as natura